---
description: Parsing or constructing shell commands must account for chaining and quoting
globs: "**/exec*.ts,**/spawn*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

When parsing or constructing shell commands:

- Do not derive "the command" by splitting the string on whitespace alone. That breaks chained commands (`&&`, `||`, `|`), quoted arguments (`echo "hello world"`), and subshells.
- Prefer passing the full command to the shell (e.g. `spawn(trimmed, [], { shell: true })`) and only derive a first-token or name when needed (e.g. for allowlists), using logic that respects quotes and stops at `|`, `&`, `;`.
